      "claim": "Prefix caching + sliding-window summary prevents quadratic session cost",
      "measured": "context slope: naive +1247 tok/turn \u2192 summarized +288 tok/turn (peak 15.6k); cost \u221247% billed (n=6 sessions per rung); quality trade-off: recall questions 2/36 vs 36/36 with cached full history, turn 1\u20133 details kept in the final summary 24/51 vs 39/51",
      "verdict": "SUPPORTED",
      "note": "Caching alone cuts cost \u221240% but context still grows +1197 tok/turn (quadratic session total). Only summarization bounds the growth. The cost claim holds, but the saving is not free: compaction drops early-turn specifics, which the assistant then declines to recall (see the quality table and the implicit-claim row)."
    },
    {
      "category": "Cat 3",
      "claim": "\u2026without losing answer quality (implicit)",
      "measured": "answers grounded (turns 1\u20139): 205/207 summarized vs 203/207 cached full history; recall questions 2/36 vs 36/36; turn 1\u20133 details in final summary 24/51 vs 39/51",
      "verdict": "NOT SUPPORTED",
      "note": "Answer key, deterministic string matching, 95% Wilson intervals. Replies on turns 1\u20139 stay grounded on every rung, but once early turns are compacted the assistant can no longer recall their specifics and the final summary keeps fewer of them. Caching alone changes no quality measure."
